# Coach speech (Swedish): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
# Always positive, never blaming. The coach says "du" to the player and "jag" of himself; nothing in
# Swedish agrees with a person's gender ("redo", "nära" are the same for everyone).
#
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level} (written to fit every sentence that inserts them):
#   appraisal.phase.*   definite nouns ("öppningen", "mittspelet", "slutspelet"): "i {text}",
#                       "{text} gick bäst", "Du spelade {text} mycket bra".
#   appraisal.reason.*  a complement right after "remi", no comma: "Remi {text}." ("Remi genom
#                       upprepning.", "Partiet slutade remi efter överenskommelse.").
#   theme.*             an infinitive phrase WITH "att", lower case, no full stop: said after a colon
#                       ("Tema: att hålla dina pjäser skyddade.") or after "öva på", "tänk på", "kom
#                       ihåg" ("Kom ihåg att ge din kung lite luft.").
#   appraisal.level.*   the coach level names of the menus (coach.level.N.name) in ”…”, said after
#                       "nivån": "redo för nivån ”Klubbspelare”".
# {opening:def} inside a sentence, {opening} alone after a colon or as the whole line.
# Move numbers: "i drag {n}" (cardinal after the noun, glossary). Accuracy: {acc:percent} = "85 %"
# (spoken "åttiofem procent") where English says "percent" or a bare number would be unclear; the
# bare number after the label "Noggrannhet" and in the terse lines, as English.
# Material won: "material värt {pts:point}" ("material worth 3 points"), never a bare "3 poäng".
# A better move that was not played takes the counterfactual "hade behållit" (English "kept").
# Never start a sentence with {n:time}: "en gång" would stay lowercase.

